WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.670
The new Pet Sematary has fans debating the
changes it made to the original story, but

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:09.440
what I've also discovered is there are some
radically different endings to the remake

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.420
that were almost used in the final film.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.900
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the three incredible

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.410
endings you never got to see in the new Pet
Sematary, including the happy ending Stephen

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.789
King recommended.

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:25.460
Plus keep watching for more deleted scenes
cut from the final film.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:28.929
Spoilers ahead for the movie, so take care
if you haven't seen it yet.

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:33.370
The filmmakers of the new Pet Sematary had
three different endings planned for the movie

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:36.270
which they describe as dark, darker and darkest.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.790
Now, the ending we actually got for the film
was pretty bleak with not just Ellie and Rachel

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:42.940
dying, but Louis also killed.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.070
On top of that, in the movie's final scene
we see the resurrected Louis, Ellie and Rachel

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.300
approaching the family's sole survivor, Gage
who's in a car looking out the window at his

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.120
undead family when we hear the horrifying
sound of the doors unlocking.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.550
The opening scene of the movie showed us an
opened car door with bloody hand stains heavily

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.570
indicating that poor Gage surely didn't survive.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:07.400
This chilling everyone-dies twist on the original
story was the darkest version on the table,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.469
and if you found it too horrifying for your
liking you might have preferred the much lighter

00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:13.689
ending that Stephen King suggested.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:18.159
The horror legend saw an "early cut" once
the filmmakers began their reshoots, and based

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:22.229
on that, he recommended "an ending where Gage
is walking up the middle of the road.

00:01:22.229 --> 00:01:25.990
We see dawn, and we hear a truck coming, and
think, 'Oh my God, he's gonna get greased

00:01:25.990 --> 00:01:26.990
in the road.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.080
That's how this is gonna end!'

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.659
[…] Then at the last second, this woman
pulls him out of the road and rescues him,

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:33.819
and says, ‘Where's your mommy and daddy?'"

00:01:33.819 --> 00:01:38.859
Both King's original story and the 1989 movie
had Gage rather than Ellie killed by a truck

00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:42.979
in the road earlier in the story, so this
alternate ending would have been a hat tip

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:46.959
to that, with the twist being this time the
little toddler is saved… at least for the

00:01:46.959 --> 00:01:47.959
time being.

00:01:47.959 --> 00:01:50.929
King would have ended the movie right there,
leaving the ultimate fate of the woman and

00:01:50.929 --> 00:01:54.600
Gage unknown as she goes off in search of
Gage's parents.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:59.221
Speaking to EW, King suggested he's "a sucker
for a happy ending" and it's interesting that

00:01:59.221 --> 00:02:03.389
the finale he suggested for the remake would
have been drastically different to how his

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.689
own book ended.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:09.350
The second alternate ending was actually filmed
and while it's still dark, it's just a touch

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:11.960
lighter than what we saw in the final movie.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.540
In an interview with Collider, producer Lorenzo
DiBonaventura describes what it entails.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:19.960
"There's a version […] where mom and daughter
are both back from the dead.

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.400
And there's a shot of [Louis] with Gage in
his lap.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.780
Both of them are normal.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.010
[…]
And then, mom walks in.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.480
She's clearly out there in another world.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.000
And daughter comes in, and daughter says,
'Hi, mommy.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.099
I love you.'

00:02:31.099 --> 00:02:34.040
And then the camera's on them like a family
portrait.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:38.500
And then it just pulls back, the little kid's
crying, and [Louis] just looks like he's been

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.940
run over by a bus."

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:43.930
So, in this version we still have an undead
Ellie and Rachel at the end, and although

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.720
it seems unlikely that Louis and Gage could
survive the onslaught of these two reanimated

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:53.680
family members, the way it ends does leave
open the slightest possibility.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.689
This alternate ending is more of a direct
play on the original 1989 movie's ending where

00:02:58.689 --> 00:03:03.290
Louis was waiting in the kitchen for the resurrected
corpse of Rachel to return to him.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:07.760
In that movie, it showed Rachel grabbing a
knife and ended on Louis's screams which is

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.470
why I think this second alternate ending for
the new film very likely implies that Louis

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:14.400
and Gage will both die.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.920
A 2017 draft of the screenplay also reveals
yet another interesting finale that could

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.920
have been.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:25.060
In this ending, it's Rachel who discovers
Jud's dead body and then goes to look for

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.290
Ellie in the woods.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:31.549
She finds her undead daughter in the Pet Sematary,
and armed with Jud's gun she tries to shoot

00:03:31.549 --> 00:03:32.569
Ellie but misses.

00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:37.680
Ellie attacks her mother with the scalpel
and during the fight Rachel drops the revolver.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.120
Ellie grabs the gun, aims it at her mother
and with pitch black eyes and a wicked smile

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.930
on her face, she says "love you mommy", then
pulls the trigger.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:50.870
But just at that moment Louis arrives, and
in the aftermath we discover he's the one

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.129
who's been shot.

00:03:52.129 --> 00:03:55.150
Louis dies leaving Rachel stricken with grief.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:59.739
The undead Ellie then walks over to her mother
and goes to kill her but notices something

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:03.689
about her mother's pain and instead whispers
something to her.

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:08.599
The scene then cuts to Gage [asleep] in the
car and suddenly Ellie's there smiling at

00:04:08.599 --> 00:04:09.599
him.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:13.930
Rachel then walks over, unlocks the car door
and takes Gage over to the front porch with

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:15.459
her where she sits down.

00:04:15.459 --> 00:04:20.720
The camera pans out to Ellie dancing in the
yard, and a shadow appears in front of her.

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.590
Ellie looks up surprised and exclaims "Daddy!"

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:25.770
At which point the screen cuts to black.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:30.139
So, as you can see, this ending like the others
is pretty crazy and twisted.

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:33.990
It's more open in terms of whether Rachel
and Gage could survive but, of course, they'd

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:36.400
need to defeat the resurrected Louis and Ellie.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:40.560
Now, if you watched the trailers for the movie,
you'll probably have noticed quite a few scenes

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.110
missing from the final film.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:46.889
For example, several Zelda scenes didn't make
it in, including this one of Zelda creeping

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:49.139
up behind Rachel and grabbing her.

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:53.110
Other Zelda scenes that were cut involve Rachel
experiencing more visions of her sister when

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:55.160
she visits her childhood home in Boston.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.710
In an interview with SlashFilm, the directors
described a deleted scene where Rachel goes

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.900
to her sister's bedroom to confront her fear
of her dead sister in a moment similar to

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.460
one in the 1989 movie.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:09.840
The reason for this cut was that the directors
"wanted to [...] focus the Zelda scenes" on

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.270
the house the family moved to in Ludlow as
by only having visions of Zelda appear to

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:19.080
Rachel in the family's new house, it emphasises
the power the Wendigo has on the area near

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.770
the cursed burial ground.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:25.400
The filmmakers also said they didn't want
the Zelda storyline to overwhelm the film,

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.430
but they've promised that we'll see these
extra scenes on the home entertainment release.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:34.139
Interestingly enough, though, Zelda wasn't
actually in the original script for the remake,

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:39.180
but when directors Kevin Kölsch &amp; Dennis
Widmyer came on board, they insisted on including

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:43.880
Zelda's story as it was vital to give Rachel
a more substantial role.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.400
There's another terrifying snippet in the
trailers that didn't make it in which looks

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.630
like a flashback to when Jud's wife Norma
was alive.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:53.860
This scene could have been really interesting
as it could have helped explain why Ellie

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:58.729
tells Jud she's seen his dead wife Norma burning
in hell for what he did to her.

00:05:58.729 --> 00:06:02.820
In King's original novel, the possessed Gage
taunts Jud about Norma cheating on him with

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.900
all his friends.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:07.190
And in the book, Jud also had a brief history
of having visited prostitutes.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:12.140
Kölsch has said that the deleted scene shows
"more of Jud's backstory, and his relationship

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.650
with the burial ground."

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:17.960
Which leads me to think that when Norma died,
Jud resurrected her, but as with everyone

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.180
who comes back Norma wasn't right.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:24.210
You can see her here rocking back and forth
in a chair while an iron has been left on

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.210
in the background.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:29.449
Jud probably had to kill the undead Norma
and now the Wendigo is using Ellie to come

00:06:29.449 --> 00:06:31.240
back as his wife to punish him.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.509
There are also some intriguing trailer scenes
of children in animal masks that never made

00:06:35.509 --> 00:06:37.140
it into the final movie.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:41.830
In the film, we only see the kids as they
parade down to the Pet Sematary, but, in the

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:45.610
trailer, there's also these additional scenes
of the children going beyond the barrier all

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:50.050
the way to the cursed burial ground where
they seem to be burying a dead animal.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:54.290
The directors have revealed that these scenes
were only filmed for marketing the movie.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:58.240
In their interview with SlashFilm, they explained
that "on studio films, they send marketing

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:02.409
departments down, and they actually have their
own camera unit, and they take your actors

00:07:02.409 --> 00:07:06.539
and go shoot things that are just specifically
for trailers, and marketing spots."

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:11.300
In fact, the directors only saw those scenes
for the first time when they saw the trailer!

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.520
They were slightly concerned that these fake
scenes, so to speak, might confuse the audience

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.039
but, in the end, they don't think they did.

00:07:18.039 --> 00:07:21.449
What do you think about any of these deleted
scenes and would you have preferred any of

00:07:21.449 --> 00:07:22.970
the alternate endings?

